{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"362e9f66bf03a952","type":"text","text":"[summary]\n\nFocus on ONLY Generative AI in program development for nonprofits.\n### Module 1: Program Development (Logic Models)\n**Learning Outcomes:**\n1. Understand the basics of nonprofit program development.\n2. Learn how to use generative AI to ideate and design new programs.\n3. Master the creation of logic models using generative AI to define program outcomes, activities, and resources.\n\n**Necessary Content:**\n- Introduction to program development in nonprofit management.\n- Overview of generative AI tools and their application in ideation and design.\n- Steps for creating a logic model: defining problem statements, objectives, inputs, activities, outputs, outcomes, and impact.\n- Case studies and examples of successful program development using generative AI.\n\n**Generative AI Use Cases:**\n- Ideation: Using AI to brainstorm and refine program ideas based on community needs and organizational goals.\n- Design: Developing program structure and activities through AI-generated templates and examples.\n- Logic Model Creation: Utilizing AI to articulate and visualize the logical flow from program resources (inputs) to the desired impact (outcomes).","x":-1560,"y":-194,"width":540,"height":914},
		{"id":"b721d13b70d028de","type":"text","text":"[topic]\nGenerative AI, ChatGPT nonprofit management, program development, logic models","x":-960,"y":-194,"width":340,"height":794},
		{"id":"61eba20dfe5938a4","type":"text","text":"[KB]\n\n{{[[Nonprofit Management (Course)]]}}","x":-41,"y":-194,"width":721,"height":754},
		{"id":"cb0c5985b7580195","type":"text","text":"[course]\n{{[[AI for Nonprofit Management (Outline)]]}}","x":-340,"y":109,"width":250,"height":264},
		{"id":"fd15b5781ca74dcf","type":"text","text":"[mod]\nModule 1\n","x":-620,"y":109,"width":250,"height":127},
		{"id":"b899d8fd05e60755","type":"text","text":"[Tone]\nProfessional, educational, engaging, practical.\n\nShow don't tell.","x":-620,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"e4ce0f2c27c7ebf7","type":"text","text":"[skills]\n\n1. **AI Literacy**: Understanding the basics of artificial intelligence, including how generative AI operates and can be applied in various nonprofit management contexts such as program development, fundraising, stewardship, and grant writing/reporting.\n    \n2. **Data Analysis and Interpretation**: Skills in analyzing and interpreting data to inform decision-making, especially in the context of donor research, program impact assessment, and identifying grant opportunities.\n    \n3. **Strategic Thinking and Planning**: Ability to use AI tools for strategic planning, including developing logic models for program development, creating targeted fundraising strategies, and planning personalized donor stewardship approaches.\n    \n4. **Creative Problem-Solving**: Leveraging AI for ideation and design, requiring creativity to solve problems and innovate within program development, fundraising campaigns, and donor engagement strategies.\n    \n5. **Technical Proficiency with AI Tools**: Competence in navigating and utilizing specific AI tools and platforms that assist in tasks such as donor segmentation, content creation for fundraising, and automated reporting.\n    \n6. **Communication and Persuasion**: Skills in crafting persuasive and engaging content with the help of AI, including writing grant proposals, fundraising appeals, and personalized donor communications.\n    \n7. **Project Management**: Managing projects effectively, from the ideation phase with AI through to execution, including organizing fundraising campaigns, overseeing program development, and handling grant reporting processes.\n    \n8. **Ethical Consideration and Bias Awareness**: Understanding the ethical implications of using AI in nonprofit management, including issues related to data privacy, donor consent, and being aware of and mitigating biases in AI-generated content and decision-making processes.\n","x":895,"y":-823,"width":810,"height":1783},
		{"id":"6b08fd22e19786b1","type":"text","text":"{{[[Project Creator]]}} create a project for {{outline}}","x":-3920,"y":4363,"width":250,"height":197,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e206a944b2d106de","type":"text","text":"### Module 1: Program Development with Generative AI in Nonprofit Management\n\n#### 1.1 Rationale: Understanding Nonprofit Program Development and Generative AI\n- The importance of effective program development in achieving nonprofit goals.\n- The transformative potential of generative AI for enhancing program development processes.\n- How mastering generative AI tools can lead to innovative solutions and increased impact in the nonprofit sector.\n\n#### 1.2 Expectations: Skills Acquisition and Application\n- Learners will be able to articulate the fundamentals of nonprofit program development.\n- Learners will gain proficiency in using generative AI for program ideation and design.\n- Learners will be competent in constructing comprehensive logic models with the assistance of generative AI.\n\n#### 1.3 Pre-Assessment: Gauging Current Understanding\n- Scenario-based questions to assess knowledge of nonprofit program development.\n- Questions on the basics of generative AI and its applications in nonprofits.\n- Logic model comprehension check to identify areas for focus in the module.\n\n#### 1.4 Concepts and Theories: Foundations of Nonprofit Program Development and Generative AI\n- Nonprofit Program Development: The lifecycle of a nonprofit program, from conception to evaluation.\n- Generative AI Overview: An introduction to generative AI, how it works, and its potential uses.\n- Logic Models Explained: The components of a logic model and their interrelationships.\n\n#### 1.5 Walkthrough: Applying Generative AI to Program Development\n- Step-by-step guide on using generative AI for program ideation, leveraging AI tools to brainstorm and refine ideas.\n- Detailed instructions on designing a program structure with AI-generated templates.\n- Creating logic models with generative AI assistance, visualizing the flow from inputs to outcomes.\n\n#### 1.6 Best Practices: Utilizing Generative AI in Nonprofit Program Development\n- Best Practices in AI-Assisted Ideation: How to use generative AI to generate and refine program ideas effectively.\n- Designing with AI: Tips for developing program structures using generative AI outputs.\n- Logic Model Construction: How to ensure clarity and coherence when building logic models with AI tools.\n\n#### 1.7 Case Study: Generative AI in Action\n- A comprehensive case study illustrating the use of generative AI in developing a nonprofit program, from ideation to logic model creation.\n- Analysis of the case study, highlighting the application of skills acquired in the module.\n- Reflection on the benefits and challenges of integrating generative AI into the program development process.\n\n#### 1.8 Application: Practicing Skills with Generative AI Tools\n- Practice Activity: Role-playing exercise using a chatbot to simulate the process of program development with generative AI.\n- Hands-on tasks for creating a draft logic model using generative AI outputs.\n- Analysis and refinement of the draft model to meet set objectives and outcomes.","x":120,"y":1880,"width":1640,"height":1600,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"6d4cb37e40c281eb","type":"text","text":"[audience]\nAdult learners looking to upskill or for a career change\n\nLittle or no experience with AI or Generative AI tools, so they need a lot of guidance and examples.\n\nThe audience will NOT be training models, only using available ones like chatgpt.","x":-340,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"18795c84f0d61402","type":"text","text":"#### 1.1 Rationale: Understanding Nonprofit Program Development and Generative AI\n\nIn the vast and dynamic sector of nonprofit management, the ability to develop impactful programs is paramount. Programs are the vehicles through which nonprofits deliver their mission to the community, address pressing issues, and create lasting change. However, crafting these programs requires strategic planning, an understanding of community needs, and the capacity to measure success. \n\nThe integration of generative AI into this process marks a significant stride forward. Generative AI refers to artificial intelligence that can generate new content based on the data it has been trained on. For nonprofits, this means the ability to automate and enhance various aspects of program development, from brainstorming ideas to creating detailed operational plans. By incorporating generative AI, nonprofits can achieve higher levels of creativity, efficiency, and effectiveness.\n\nFor those in the nonprofit sector, learning to harness the capabilities of generative AI is not just an exercise in technical proficiency; it is about embracing a tool that can amplify impact. Imagine a scenario where you can instantly generate a range of potential solutions to a community problem, draft grant proposals, or even create personalized communication materials for your audience—all with the support of AI.\n\nThe benefits of mastering generative AI tools are multifaceted:\n- **Efficiency**: Automating tasks that traditionally take up considerable time allows staff to focus on strategic decisions and human-centered work.\n- **Innovation**: Generative AI can provide unexpected perspectives and ideas, pushing the boundaries of traditional program design.\n- **Precision**: AI tools can assist in creating more accurate and data-driven logic models, leading to better alignment of activities and desired outcomes.\n\nFor those aiming to make a significant impact in their nonprofit roles, understanding and utilizing generative AI is not just advantageous—it is becoming essential. This module will equip you with the knowledge and skills to be at the forefront of this technological advancement, ensuring that your programs resonate with both the heart and the intelligence of what AI can offer.","x":-2600,"y":1880,"width":888,"height":1147,"color":"6"},
